CDN vs CloudFront
CDN and CloudFront are related, but they are not the same thing.
CDN (Content Delivery Network) is a network of geographically distributed servers used to deliver cached content closer to users.
CloudFront is AWS's CDN service used to create and manage a CDN for your application.
❌ “CloudFront creates an Edge Location.”
Better: ✅ “CloudFront uses AWS's existing Edge Locations and manages the CDN through them.”
CloudFront → the AWS service managing the whole CDN.
CDN → the delivery/caching system provided by CloudFront.
Edge Location → the server/location where the content is cached and served to users.
CloudFront creates/manages the CDN infrastructure for you. ✅
Distributed servers = servers spread across different locations around the world, so users can get content from a nearby server.

In CloudFront, these geographically distributed locations are called Edge Locations.
Sure. In “CloudFront is used to create and manage a CDN”, these two words mean:

