One-line memory trick

Images, CSS, JS → CloudFront can cache and serve from the nearest edge.

Login, Orders, Payments → CloudFront forwards the request to the origin/backend for processing.

So in your example, yes: if the origin is in the USA and the user is in India, the first uncached static request reaches the USA origin through 
CloudFront, while later cached requests are served from the nearby India edge.


